---
import Container from "@components/elements/Container.astro";
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About the UMASD Accountability Project and its author."
>
  <Container class="py-12 sm:py-16 lg:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-10">

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">About this project</h1>
        <p class="text-base text-base-content/70 sm:text-lg">
          An independent, data-driven analysis of Upper Merion Area School District
          administrative decisions and their impact on students.
        </p>
      </div>

    <div class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Who I am</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-start">
        <img
        src="/images/doug.jpg"
        alt="Doug Scheesley"
        class="h-28 w-28 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full object-cover"
        />
        <div class="space-y-4">
        <p class="text-base text-base-content/70">
            My name is Doug Scheesley. I am a parent of a student at Bridgeport Elementary School 
            and a chemist by training, with a professional background in data analysis, root cause 
            analysis, and software engineering. I built this site on my own time, using my own 
            skills, and at my own expense.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base text-base-content/70">
            This project is not affiliated with the BES PTC, UMASD, or any other organization.
            The views and analysis presented here are entirely my own, based on publicly available 
            records and Right to Know data obtained independently and in coordination with other 
            concerned community members.
        </p>
        </div>
    </div>
    </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Why I did this</h2>
        <p class="text-base text-base-content/70">
          In the 2025–26 school year, my child's second grade class reached 28 students —
          well beyond the 24-student class size guidance the district had established for
          elementary education. When I sought answers, the explanations offered by district
          administration did not hold up to scrutiny.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base text-base-content/70">
          I am trained in root cause analysis and have spent my career solving problems by
          following evidence rather than assumption. I applied that same methodology here.
          The data the district holds is public record. The analytical techniques are
          standard. The conclusions follow from the evidence.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base text-base-content/70">
            I built this site because I believe parents and community members deserve access to 
            clear, honest analysis presented without agenda. If the work here is wrong, I welcome 
            correction. If it is right, I hope it leads to better outcomes for every student in 
            the district.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">A note on bias</h2>
        <p class="text-base text-base-content/70">
          I am a parent of a student directly impacted by the class size issue analyzed
          here. Every effort has been made to present the evidence objectively and avoid
          emotionally charged arguments. Bias is inherent to human nature, and I encourage
          anyone reading this work to evaluate it critically and on its own merits.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Contact</h2>
            <p class="text-base text-base-content/70">
            You can reach me at{" "}
            <a href="mailto:douglas.scheesley@gmail.com" class="link link-primary">
                douglas.scheesley@gmail.com
            </a>{" "}
            or find me on{" "}
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/douglas-scheesley-48558517/" class="link link-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                LinkedIn
            </a>.
            </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>